{"title":"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(similar_to_1,_different_ending)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (similar to 1, different ending)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of ordered triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factor\" title=\"Factor\">factor</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/0/08056d020dbdf873ea85ac38de7d2bc46d7e5834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/a/8aae210987efa7516252487e71424146bd925807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{b}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/9/799e8e40f26c6255ff30857b16e4b07779937c76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{c}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"33\" />. The last condition reduces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/35418abe4b3b62c22de394b4ff32cf5c8c760e5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(1 + x + y) = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b99b89387766ebe13be834aecad6e274a0b49c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + x + y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" /> is equal to one of the 9 factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/3/a933ab10c4ca53ffc10144c5193ba098cd3a367e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 = 2^25^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Subtracting the one, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/a/8fab4bb936ce33be4dec4440b1bf0fd21081b365.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = \\{0,1,3,4,9,19,24,49,99\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"266\" height=\"18\" />. There are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e80c6b6a84ad4015ea436a915435d69edbdd96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> ways to find pairs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/1431708d213aff4b13b068d6a2da358e8f07b2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3fb9066c1164195a8fa1a456602bc464a9b564.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 + 0 + 2 + 3 + 8 + 18 + 23 + 48 + 98 = \\boxed{200}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"359\" height=\"23\" /> solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Alternatively, note that the sum of the divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a724d92713ad82ff9738a7dc6dc601eafc36c4c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 + 2 + 2^2)(1 + 5 + 5^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"21\" /> (notice that after distributing, every divisor is accounted for). This evaluates to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f7e38df51daaf467517be6d3a8f2207727e9cb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\cdot 31 = 217$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />. Subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/5029c3f6fed512b6a8ab1b39a8a2ae617e49dd65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\cdot 2$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> for reasons noted above to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f31ff033089cb9cfa5a6ce6cd9a0ce6b5c57422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$199$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. Finally, this changes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e8005b4b33e3ee72ec914848735f8fc473b08877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\Rightarrow -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" />, so we have to add one to account for that. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/4/d54c01bf8b58951d7f6775fa650b26155f55102c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{200}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28similar_to_1.2C_different_ending.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(similar_to_1,_different_ending)\">Solution 2 (similar to 1, different ending)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (similar to 1, different ending)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d860cd35e3a476041559922536fd43588f890ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = ak$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65b5fcc57f99f560b1ceab277dd81cb6e58b1fa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = aj$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/f/47fdca862c9993d9ebbc253d7f45473c10f091a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k,j \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+ \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/f/d2fdb27c8e0f85666880d66574152ccbc1510ef6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b,c \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />. Then, factoring out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/5/355d45a5683ca12a6029c4a991e33bc3a0768b78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(1+x+y) = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, and so is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/c/60c4e94c8e3c27e67fc790d07f9a5632832b062e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" /> by definition, so that implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/8/b4810500e837ac4fab013f1cffee31ed391beeb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ | \\ 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"20\" />. The possible choices for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f0179f77334c0d2a9cabd24d6f7513ca47b3bdd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 4, 5, 10, 20, 25, 50, 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"203\" height=\"17\" />. Each of those gives options <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/00192a5925dd5954c5b0813cc906fe3a1d204de0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+j = 0,1,3,4,9,19,24,49,99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"250\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. Negate 0 and 1 as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> are positive integers not equal to 0. While we can attempt to find through exclusion stars and bars the number of ways as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79ede376e2cd5bb43a5c6f3c5e18dcb02ac49198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{x-1}{y-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"72\" height=\"55\" />, coming to the realization that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851018537a4268dffd3e893158af5b7d9f3aeb0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> will always be 1 (as we have 2 variables <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/4/8a4ddfe00ca134641093f40f423ed8492a6eeb49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k,j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />), and continuing by solution 1, we could also constructively overcount. By stars and bars, each two equations will have integer solutions, inclusive 0, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7dcafe4cf1d8ed2018f7e64c710fdaded9a12e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{x+y-1}{y-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"103\" height=\"55\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/a/40ac4b6f5ab516ac6fe7132ed2fe7a1d77ca02dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> forces the bottom of the binomial as 1, making it expendable and therefore we just consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/6/946c2538d06e0fa0de538b309c43ed932897f619.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" />. Here, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad9e63fe44ba87b28cb3dc3f21f19ea932144b28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" /> so we just consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> cases total, so we sum over ALL terms and obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/4/8541a6a25d20e7caa8c806afdd2d3656a1f26cf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100+50+25+20+10+5+4 = 214$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"305\" height=\"15\" />. However, 14 of these cases are invalid, particularly, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/48228b9ab6ce87d12ff56325e0b3f6abaeaa5bd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+j = 3,4,9,19,24,49,99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" />, and one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> is 0. There are two choice for which variable is 0, and 7 total <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/f/acfe39b51b84a4ef24d48608160b72692f72f240.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> values, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdc6504874eea6b913d2861882643c9cbd94c792.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 7 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /> of the total that do not work, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a98e06d958b9c450e9eb03edaac8955f55758cd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$214 - 14 = \\boxed{200}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"132\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/LqrXinQbk1Q?t=73\">https://youtu.be/LqrXinQbk1Q?t=73</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II\" title=\"2007 AIME II\">2007 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2007\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016224921\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 363/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10062/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.331      1 -total\n 61.04%    8.138      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.26%    4.967      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4808:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016224921 and revision id 284723. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}